{"id": "EUVD-2026-104317", "enisaUuid": "e8eab5ce-1ed2-39df-a1f4-2fe2108697be", "description": "Mopidy before 4.0.5 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated clients to access local files outside file/media_dirs because FileLibraryProvider.lookup() lacks a containment check. Attackers can call core.library.lookup or core.tracklist.add over JSON-RPC or WebSocket with file:// URIs to probe file existence, read tag metadata, and play out-of-sandbox files.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T14:24:41", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/mopidy/mopidy/issues/2350", "https://github.com/mopidy/mopidy/commit/f23c1f8621c3f4eb07a35d37fccb597449d36415", "https://github.com/mopidy/mopidy/blob/v4.0.4/src/mopidy/_exts/file/library.py", "https://github.com/mopidy/mopidy/releases/tag/v4.0.5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mopidy-before-4.0.5-path-traversal-via-file-backend-library-lookup"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111925", "GHSA-p8f3-3m4r-p796"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ca20634-ca1d-3804-a988-37d9b54915da", "product": {"name": "Mopidy", "vendor": {"name": "Mopidy"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.0.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bf571b36-2d02-3aab-ae8e-e25522271134", "vendor": {"name": "Mopidy"}}], "isExploited": false}